Backports of three upstream frontend fixes onto vLLM 0.31.0 (API-server side only: tool-call parser and detokenizer;
no engine, GPU or model-output change; no new knob, always on):
  #64675 (Qwen3 tool-call parser: parse each closed <parameter> once while streaming; follow-up to #62027. Merged
          upstream. Hand-merged into this stack's _qwen3_arg_converter, which also carries #59882: </function> is
          stripped first, then the cached parse runs with partial = partial or call_closed.)
  #65775 (fixes #65774: a repeated Qwen3 tool parameter keeps its FIRST value, so streamed arguments stay valid JSON
          and equal the non-streaming ones. Open upstream. Behaviour change: non-streaming used to keep the LAST value.
          The unclosed last parameter kept by #59882 follows the same first-value rule.)
  #63668 (fixes #63667: cap the tokens the incremental detokenizers hold back on malformed UTF-8 at
          MAX_PENDING_TOKENS = 16 and flush them as U+FFFD, instead of re-decoding the whole run on every token. Open
          upstream. v1/engine/detokenizer.py as upstream; in detokenizer_utils.py upstream's output_token_count, a local
          0.31 does not have, is written len(output_tokens).)
Tests (CPU, PYTHONPATH at a patched copy of the installed package; no server was run):
  tests/parser (0.31 suite + earlier PRs' tests, cohere/ and mistral/ ignored as before): 4882 passed, 2 skipped
  before and after; with the 10 tests of #64675/#65775 added: 4892 passed, 2 skipped (8 of the 10 fail unpatched).
  tests/tokenizers_/test_detokenize.py (v0.31.0 file, -k "not Llama-3.2 and not Pixtral and not mistral"): 500 passed,
  160 skipped before and after; with #63668's 6 tests added: 506 passed, 160 skipped.
  Timing, CodeLlama-7b tokenizer, N lone lead-byte tokens after a prompt, 1000/2000/4000/8000 tokens:
    fast, before 0.078/0.305/1.205/5.463 s (nothing streamed); after 0.005/0.010/0.021/0.042 s
    slow, before 0.082/0.328/1.174/4.628 s (nothing streamed); after 0.025/0.052/0.115/0.283 s
    (slow rows with len(tokenizer) cached in the benchmark: 0.31 calls it on every slow step, ~4 ms each with a
    fast tokenizer, a constant this patch leaves alone and that otherwise hides the difference)
  Differential fuzz: converter/extender with and without the closed-parameter cache, and against the unpatched
  converter on duplicate-free input, 0 mismatches in ~100K growth steps; streamed == non-streaming arguments in
  9000 runs of random calls with repeated and unclosed parameters.

